  {
   "id": 632143,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>Lin is solving this system of equations:</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\begin {cases} 6x-5y=34\\\\3x+2y=8 \\end {cases}\">\\begin {cases} 6x-5y=34\\\\3x+2y=8 \\end {cases}</span></p>\n<p>She starts by rearranging the second equation to isolate the <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> variable: <span data-math=\"y = 4 - 1.5x\">y = 4 - 1.5x</span>. She then substitutes the expression <span data-math=\"4 - 1.5x\">4 - 1.5x</span> for <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> in the first equation, as shown:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"6x-5(4-1.5x)=34\">6x-5(4-1.5x)=34</span><br><span data-math=\"6x-20-7.5x=34\">6x-20-7.5x=34</span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"-1.5x=54\">-1.5x=54</span><br> <span data-math=\"x=-36\">x=-36</span><br></p>\n <br> <p><span data-math=\"y=4-1.5x\">y=4-1.5x</span><br></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y=4-1.5 \\cdot(-36)\">y=4-1.5 \\cdot(-36)</span><br></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y=58\">y=58</span></p>\n<p>Does Lin’s solution of <span data-math=\"(-36, 58)\">(-36, 58)</span> makes both equations in the system true?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1223866,
     "content_html": "No; Her solution does not make both equations true."
    },
    {
     "id": 1223865,
     "content_html": "yes; Her solution makes both equations true."
    }
   ],
